c(13, "§3.1 table (verbatim); §3.1", "insight", "The prioritised picture (verbatim): " + table("## 3.1 The prioritised picture", 0) + " — six findings carry the corpus: delight in simplicity (praise_any 476, 77.52%); outcomes including recovery (outcome_any 118, safety_sensitive 23); requests from satisfied users (request_any 164, 26.71%, 4.45★, led by the widget); reliability (crash_any 65, all but one in one week); ads (ads_negative 20, including gambling ads); goals (goal_setting 25 — a fixed ladder users cannot understand or change); negative_any 119 (19.38%, 2.59★).", "n/a", "mixed", "praise_any 476; outcome_any 118; request_any 164; crash_any 65; ads_negative 20; goal_setting 25; negative_any 119", "none", "table", "generalisable", ["10508150052", "14309392133"], "", "")

c(14, "§3.2 table (verbatim); §3.2", "feature", "What people value (verbatim): " + table("## 3.2 What people value", 0) + " — simple and convenient (SIMPLE_EASY 132, 4.91★: 'no subscriptions and no extra buttons'); the number is the motivation (COUNTER_PROGRESS 48, 4.94★: a reviewer who dreams of smoking is 'horrified at having to log attempt 2 in the app'); design that stays out of the way (DESIGN 39: 'the idea of the tree as the main icon is simply beautiful'); free and several habits at once (FREE 30, MULTI_HABITS 17, NO_FEW_ADS 19: 'so far the best free app I've found', ua); the relapse note (NOTES_LOG 21, 4.90★: 'the ability to write and save the reason when you relapse is wonderful', jp, severe phone addiction; a Ukrainian reviewer notes a slip instead of resetting — 'I didn't want one day's slip to wipe two weeks, so I just noted the day'); best in category 20; generic praise 184 with 281 reviews under 60 characters.", "counter + relapse note + several habits, free", "praise", "SIMPLE_EASY 132 / 21.50%; COUNTER_PROGRESS 48; DESIGN 39; FREE 30; NOTES_LOG 21; BEST 20; NO_FEW_ADS 19; MULTI_HABITS 17; ARTICLES 3; LOCALISATION 3; FIX_CONFIRMED 1", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11385749806", "12237576860", "14274384633", "12265272270", "11090976286", "12305497364"], "", "users route around a punitive reset by logging the slip as a note — the note is the forgiveness mechanic the product lacks")

c(15, "§3.3 table (verbatim); §3.3", "insight", "Outcomes (verbatim): " + table("## 3.3 Outcomes", 0) + " — quit or abstaining (OUT_QUIT_ABSTAINING 42, 6.84%, 4.86★: 'not smoking for 2 years', ua, quit the day she installed it; 'quit smoking and drugs with the app'); helps and motivates (80, 13.03%, 4.94★, often a single word 'помогает'); relapse and limits — OUT_NOT_HELPED_RELAPSE 11 (1.79%), all at five stars ('it didn't help me, but 5 stars because it's pretty'; 'no app will rid you of a bad habit — only you'; 'I love logging a new binge here every other day').", "n/a", "praise", "HELPS_MOTIVATES 80 / 13.03%; QUIT_ABSTAINING 42 / 6.84%; NOT_HELPED 11 (all 5★)", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13909943404", "12061048113", "13446644177", "14000029981", "14374645778"], "", "")

c(16, "§3.4 table (verbatim); §3.4", "audience", "What people quit and who they are (verbatim): " + table("## 3.4 What people quit", 0) + " — use_named_any 61 (9.93%): smoking or vaping 17, self-harm 13, other habits 12 (phone addiction, face picking, nail and lip biting, swearing, a habit that caused stuttering, sins), alcohol 10, drugs 8, food or weight 8, sexual 3; substance_any 31 (5.05%); switchers SEG_TRIED_OTHERS 17 (4.76★) and one named competitor — 'what Clean Day lacked!' (relapse tracking and statistics); long-term users SEG_LONG_TENURE 8 ('using it 3 years'); the developer's other apps DEV_OTHER_APPS 5 ('downloaded all your apps'; wants widgets 'across the whole trilogy'); ACQ_SOCIAL 2.", "n/a", "mixed", "use_named 61 / 9.93%; SMOKING 17; SELF_HARM 13; OTHER 12; ALCOHOL 10; DRUGS 8; FOOD 8; TRIED_OTHERS 17; LONG_TENURE 8; DEV_OTHER_APPS 5", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["11090976286", "11805498745", "13571385085", "13372482805", "13435697404", "14031927743", "14508535798", "13691453399", "13608827260", "14095730161", "11651806786", "12899775386"], "", "")

c(17, "§3.5 table (verbatim); §3.5", "must-never-break", "Reliability (verbatim): " + table("## 3.5 Reliability", 0) + " — defect_any 70 (11.40%, 2.34★), crash_any 65; the crash week: devices named include iPhone 13, 14, 14 Pro Max on iOS 26.5.2 and iPhone 17 Pro; reinstalling did not help; CRASH_OFFLINE_WORKAROUND 3; counter errors BUG_COUNTER_ATTEMPTS 5 — the count follows the phone clock ('changing the phone's date changes the count'), attempt 2 not recorded, a deleted relapse still counts, a wrong day count after the update; lost data DATA_LOSS 3 (kept on data-loss grounds: 'and it deleted itself'; 'don't open it for a week and it reset day 1000 to zero'; the crash-week loss); thin product FEATURE_THIN 12 (3.33★: 'just a timer: start, stop'; 'no more complex than a timer'); maintenance NEGLECT_PERCEIVED 3, all during the 19 months without a release ('will there be updates? judging by the last one, I feel I shouldn't wait'); REDESIGN_DISLIKE 1 ('the old design was better; why add an archive button?').", "counter keyed to device clock; silent reset of a 1000-day streak", "complaint", "defect_any 70 / 11.40%; CRASH 65; AFTER_UPDATE 21; CRASH_AD_LOAD 14; FEATURE_THIN 12; COUNTER_ATTEMPTS 5; UX_CONFUSING 5; DATA_LOSS 3; NEGLECT 3; REDESIGN 1", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14317316998", "14326924586", "14325996890", "14330378148", "11644642764", "11876692458", "13755233141", "14316874234", "11194993574", "12207978135", "14313036902", "13964268722", "10960263124", "12867989318", "14371521430"], "", "")

c(18, "§3.6 table (verbatim); §3.6", "monetization", "Free tier, ads and paywall perception (verbatim): " + table("## 3.6 Free tier, ads and paywall", 0) + " — monetisation_friction 28 (4.56%, 2.61★); ads — ADS_TOO_MANY 18 (2.72★): 'a long ad after every action; deleting'; 'the ads are long and can't be skipped'; some accept it ('far too many ads in the free version, but it's pointless complaining', 4★; 'the ads are fully justified', 5★); gambling ads 2; fear of future monetisation 3 ('just don't ruin it with ads'; 'no ads, which is good; I hope none appear'); perceived paywall 6 ('or is it only in the paid version?'; 'the app is good, pity it's paid', 5★); subscription objection 2 ('a measly 100₽ on a subscription, and I just deleted the app'); PRICE_FAIR 1.", "unskippable interstitials in a free app; no lifetime", "complaint", "monetisation_friction 28 / 4.56%; ADS_TOO_MANY 18 / 2.72★; PAYWALL_PERCEIVED 6; FUTURE_WORRY 3; SUBSCRIPTION_OBJECTION 2; WANT_ONE_TIME 2; HARMFUL 2; PRICE_FAIR 1", "none", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["14205925648", "13521151325", "13822626598", "14508678503", "10683386706", "13712536946", "10306903519", "13840823158", "12839988426"], "", "")

c(19, "§3.7 table (verbatim); §3.7", "must-have", "Goals (verbatim): " + table("## 3.7 Goals", 0) + " — goal_setting 25 (4.07%, 4.12★), a request from people who otherwise like the app; the ladder confuses new users ('tapped everything, can't see where to change the goal', 3★; 'spent the first day trying to understand why my goal is one day and where to change it'); the steps don't fit (7 then 30 days too far for strong habits; 'a 100-year goal is somewhat unrealistic', de; 'it sets a month automatically, I need a year'); some like it automatic ('I like that the goal updates automatically and gives a push', 5★).", "auto-stepping goal ladder, not editable, not explained", "request", "STEPS_RIGID 15 / 2.44%; HOWTO_QUESTION 13 / 2.12%; goal_setting 25 / 4.07% / 4.12★", "must-have", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["12689955719", "12867989318", "11823352857", "14456135031", "13445493559", "13793876521"], "", "")

c(20, "§3.8 table (verbatim); §3.8", "feature", "Requests (verbatim): " + table("## 3.8 Requests", 0) + " — request_any 164 (26.71%, 4.45★), request_not_widget 90 (14.66%); widget 86 — lock screen, home screen, with the day count and the wheel, and to mark progress ('add widgets and it will be the best app in the category'); tree growth 28, with 8 reviews citing other reviews (META_CITES_OTHER_REVIEWS 8: 'I'll voice everyone's request: PLEASE ADD TREE GROWTH'); motivation content 14 — achievements, quotes, supportive relapse copy ('show a line saying how many days you could have been clean'; 'a button for almost relapsed'); notifications 11 ('Only downside is no notifications'; 'the app is forgotten very quickly'); colours/themes 7 ('the colours are too toxic'); notes editing 7; counter display 5 ('annoying that there's no day count for the current attempt'); calendar 4 ('relapses as dots on a calendar'); relapse options 4 ('you can't pause and keep your progress'); backup/sync 4 ('if I change iPhone, will my progress be saved?'); benefits stats 3 ('bad that it doesn't show cigarettes or drinks not consumed'); sort order 4; positive habits 3 ('the words refusal, bad habits, relapse are so-so'); other 4.", "n/a", "request", "request_any 164 / 26.71%; WIDGET 86; TREE_GROWTH 28; MOTIVATION_CONTENT 14; NOTIFICATIONS 11; COLOURS 7; NOTES_EDITING 7; COUNTER_DISPLAY 5; CALENDAR 4; RELAPSE_OPTIONS 4; BACKUP_SYNC 4; SORT 4; OTHER 4; BENEFITS 3; POSITIVE_HABITS 3; CITES_OTHER_REVIEWS 8", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["9590848342", "10929591148", "11317075866", "12930342553", "13070652861", "13724399997", "13716590558", "11591085925", "11836674599", "13511567781", "14234441517", "10995642477", "14118955087", "11481446444", "11959471388", "10843849305", "11058579544", "14380495771", "12031517995", "12780782479", "12774617599", "11848596914"], "", "")

c(21, "§3.9 table (verbatim); §3.9 churn table (verbatim); §3.9", "must-have", "Support, trust and churn (verbatim): " + table("## 3.9 Support, trust and churn", 0) + " || churn (verbatim): " + table("## 3.9 Support, trust and churn", 1) + " — SUPPORT_QUESTION 15 (2.44%), 14 of them RU: how to set the goal, the start date, whether progress transfers, how to fix the crash; no reviewer mentions a reply; lost_user_signal 13 (2.12%, 1.92★) — CHURN_STATED 11 with stated reasons: ads (6), the crash (2), no widget, nothing happening in the app, a charge after cancelling; SCAM_LANGUAGE 4: 'deception' over an unexpected charge (tr), 'scam' over gambling ads, 'greedy' (co), 'the reviews seem bought'.", "no visible reply channel; questions land in reviews", "churn", "SUPPORT_QUESTION 15 (ru 14); CHURN_STATED 11 / 1.73★ (ads 6, crash 2, widget 1); SCAM 4; CHURN_RISK 2; COMP_NAMED 1", "must-have", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["10306903519", "12780782479", "11675365714", "12346475330", "13116009951", "14205925648", "14326452102", "14332778196", "14103004927", "13305706545", "13524890756", "10097280052", "13174041563", "11374484206", "10856120064"], "", "")

c(22, "§3.10 table (verbatim); §3.10 billing table (verbatim); §3.10", "monetization", "Billing and paid users (verbatim): " + table("## 3.10 Billing and paid users", 0) + " || billing (verbatim): " + table("## 3.10 Billing and paid users", 1) + " — WOULD_PAY_INTENT 3 (all 5★: conditional on widgets; wants a lifetime purchase); PAID_EXPLICIT 2, both satisfied, both ad removal; TRIAL_USER 1; BILL_UNEXPECTED_CHARGE 2 (1.00★): the listing 'says completely free', then money was taken and a refund requested (tr, 2023); 'even though I deleted it and cancelled, they still try to charge me for the free subscription' (ru, 2025-12).", "ad-removal subscription with a trial; charge attempts after cancel", "mixed", "WOULD_PAY 3; PAID 2 / satisfied 2; TRIAL_USER 1; UNEXPECTED_CHARGE 2 / 1.00★; REFUND_REQUEST 1", "none", "Weak", "generalisable", ["10456809560", "11505099084", "11641762030", "11651806786", "13254705653", "13524890756", "10097280052"], "", "")

c(23, "§3.11", "must-have", "Privacy and safety: USE_SELF_HARM 13 (2.12%, 4.92★) — 12 of 13 describe stopping or holding back, one a lapse ('of course the urge doesn't go, but at least I don't hurt myself'; 'with it I stopped crying and cutting', ua, 2023-12); USE_DRUGS 8 — cocaine, injected drugs, Lyrica ('held out less than a day but the app is great'), weed; two may be jokes; relapse copy is emotionally loaded for this audience — a relapse wipes the counter and users ask for supportive wording; gambling ads (§0.6); no reviewer raises privacy, tracking or data against a label that declares data used to track.", "relapse wipes the counter; ad label declares tracking", "mixed", "SELF_HARM 13 / 4.92★ (12 holding back); DRUGS 8; privacy concern 0", "must-have", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["13346175054", "10764145523", "12210270920", "13946108990", "13960493073", "13744886789", "13807541941"], "", "")

c(24, "§4.1 table (verbatim); §4.1; §4.2 table (verbatim); §4.2", "data-caveat", "Distribution (verbatim): " + table("## 4.1 The distribution", 0) + " — mean 4.397★, median 5★, 71.50% five-star, 10.10% one- or two-star vs public 4.913★; themes by band (verbatim): " + table("## 4.2 Themes by star band", 0) + " — 'the bands are about different things': five stars is praise (93%) and short text (51%); four stars is praise plus a request (30 of 87 widget, 15 tree growth); three stars and below is the crash (46% / 71% / 62%) and ads; helpful votes rise as ratings fall (5% of five-star carry votes, 27% of one-star).", "n/a", "mixed", "5★ 439 (71.50%); 4★ 87; 1★ 45 (7.33%); public 4.913★", "none", "table", "generalisable", ["12636973228"], "", "")

c(25, "§4.3; §4.4; §4.5; §4.6", "data-caveat", "By band: 5★ (439) — 408 praise (93%), outcomes in 111 (25%), 225 under 60 characters, 52 ask for a widget and 12 for tree growth while giving five stars, 5 are crash reports and 4 complaint-only ('crashes endlessly' at 5★); 4★ (87) — 'Good, but add…': 53 praise, 37 (43%) make a non-widget request, widget 30 and tree growth 15 are the missing star, goal_setting peaks here (15%), 8 crash reports; 3★ (26) — broken, still liked: 12 crash (46%), 10 praise, 5 monetisation friction (ads and a subscription; no lifetime ad removal; gambling ads); 2★/1★ (62) — 40 crash reports, all in the crash week; 12 of 45 one-star carry monetisation friction (27%), 8 name ads; the 12 that are neither crash nor ads: an unexpected charge (2), a perceived full paywall (2), the app dismissed as just a timer (3), no widget, no tree growth after years, a redesign, and two positive texts at one or two stars.", "n/a", "mixed", "5★ requests widget 52; 4★ non-widget requests 43%; 3★ crash 46%; 1–2★ crash 40 of 62", "none", "table", "generalisable", ["14314900938", "12636973228", "12839988426", "14162589436", "12635810456", "10097280052", "13524890756", "10856120064", "11890941612", "10960263124", "13305706545", "13964268722", "11448181173", "12966085325", "14371521430", "12305474577", "14294362470"], "", "")

c(26, "§4.7 table (verbatim); §4.7", "contradiction", "Rating-versus-text contradictions (verbatim): " + table("## 4.7 Rating-versus-text contradictions", 0) + " — META_RATING_TEXT_MISMATCH 16 (2.61%), retained; 14 of 16 are four- or five-star reviews with only a complaint — 7 crash reports posted during the crash week, others about ads, the widget or a counter bug; the other two are praise at one or two stars ('helped me quit' at 1★; 'the app's fine' at 2★) — 'low stars in this corpus track the crash, not dissatisfaction with the product's concept'.", "n/a", "mixed", "MISMATCH 16 / 2.61%; complaint-only 4–5★ 14; praise at 1–2★ 2", "none", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["11876692458", "12305474577", "13152526034", "13420117881", "13643213864", "13822626598", "14103004927", "14294362470", "14312752399", "14314900938", "14315634850", "14317316998", "14317775575", "14329073914", "14331731205", "14334827225"], "", "")

